{quote}So that legal can help in this situation, there is a need to understand in general what is the business position in such cases? Are we willing to provide requested compensations or try to agree on lower amounts? Or are we very strict in denying them?{quote}

CS cannot answer what our business position is. This is something for Legal and Local OPS to decide.

{quote}By the way, how did you find out that the incident does not meet our threshold for insurance coverage? Please clarify the mechanism here.{quote}

Insurance coverage requires a minimum of 15% permanent disability caused by an accident ([https://bolt.eu/de-de/legal/personal-accident/?category=insurance|https://bolt.eu/de-de/legal/personal-accident/?category=insurance|smart-link] ). The injuries of the user did not lead to a permanent disability, so that they are not covered.

{quote}Also, could you please specify, if the same e-scooter was used by another user after the incident but before the e-scooter was repaired/adjusted by us? Were there any reports on bad operation of the e-scooter from another users close before and after the incident?{quote}

The brakes of the scooter were repaired/adjusted two days after the accident. No bad feedback from [the order before the accident|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/rentals-micromobility/orders/edit/germany/167647539?tab=details] and one negative feedback for [the order after the accident|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/rentals-micromobility/orders/edit/germany/167703964?tab=details].



