[~accountid:641d5e830e6828ab20269e6d] please see my answers in green below:


* Am I correct that age verification requirement lies directly with Bolt as a retailer, not the legal entity selling tobacco? {color:#36b37e}It is quite complex. The seller is the one who must provide the Slovak Register with the description of the age verification mechanism (Bolt is not required to report it). But since it is the Bolt Food platform which is used as a “communication channel” among the providers, the couriers and the customers, the responsibility for age verification system is shared. This is what the external counsel advised but I found this “shared responsibility” as “contractual liability” because the Slovak tobacco regulations apply much more to the seller than to the platforms. Our external counsel recommends that the Bolt Food platform ensures that the age verification system meets the obligations. {color}
* How are we gonna phrase it in the T&Cs, eg who is responsible for the age verification? {color:#36b37e}Bolt shall be responsible for technical feasibility of the age verification mechanism on the platform. However, at the stage of delivery: The courier is under a legal obligation to refuse delivery to minors. Nonetheless, the ultimate responsibility and liability for age verification rest with the seller.{color}
* Based on the above, we would understand what the role of Bolt is: controller (as a retailer who is obliged to check the age), the processor (who is facilitating age check for a tobacco seller) and what the role of couriers is - processors on behalf of Bolt or a seller. {color:#36b37e}As far as I am concerned the couriers should be processors on behalf of the sellers.{color}
* I’ve noticed in the ticket that (i) blurred item, (ii) checkbox, (iii) courier verification in place is not enough by law, but our competitors are doing this. Did the business agree to make an ID verification instead of what our competitors are doing? {color:#36b37e}You mean at the stage of purchasing process in SK? Could you please give some examples? Our external did clearly say that at purchasing such mechanism is not sufficient and needs ID ver. But for the mare displaying/promotional purposes, these measures (blurring, checkbox) are enough. Anyway, I will reach out to {color}[~accountid:623ace2e9b54ec0068b09d10] {color:#36b37e}on  awareness of the business practice and his position towards it. {color}:loading: 
* I see there is a requirement to show to the STI the age verification flow before we implement it into the product (main ticket analysis). Is this correct? If yes, what is the deadline to show it, so our team can review the prepared document?  {color:#36b37e}Yes, confirm that the seller must disclose the age verification system to the STI before the online sale gets started. However, there is not specified term of such reporting. I assume that the seller  must submit the age-verification system description together with the registration documents to the STI, i.e., before commencing the sales of tobacco in Slovakia. Then, deadline TBC with business and the seller.{color}

